# Shared environment for the trex systemd units (EnvironmentFile=/etc/trex/trex.env).
# JVM options applied to every trex process.
#
# Logging: each service ships a simplelogger.properties defaulting to info on stderr,
# which journald captures. A system property here overrides it without a rebuild —
# append it to JAVA_OPTS and restart the unit, e.g.
#
#   JAVA_OPTS=-Xms64m -Xmx512m -XX:+UseSerialGC -Dorg.slf4j.simpleLogger.defaultLogLevel=debug
#
# Levels: error, warn, info (default), debug, trace. debug adds per-append head offsets,
# 4xx responses and SSE connect/disconnect; trace adds every fold transition, which is one
# line per journal line on replay — useful for a post-mortem, far too loud to leave on.
# Per-logger overrides raise one logger without the rest, e.g. to watch only the journal
# write path:  -Dorg.slf4j.simpleLogger.log.trex.sequencer.journal.JsonlJournal=debug
#
# Values must not contain spaces: systemd splits $JAVA_OPTS on whitespace.
JAVA_OPTS=-Xms64m -Xmx512m -XX:+UseSerialGC
